'''NOPW Wednesday Episode 5''' was the fifth weekly [[Wednesday Night Wrestling|Wednesday night]] professional wrestling event produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], held on July 22, 2026 at the Okayama Prefectural Arena in [[Anjo-Saikawa]], [[Okayama Prefecture]]. The event was the first NOPW show held in Okayama and the fifth consecutive Wednesday night event in a different city, following [[Nagayama]] (Episode 1), [[Kurosaki]] (Episode 2), [[Tosa]] (Episode 3), and [[Naruto, Naruto|Naruto]] (Episode 4). The show completed the Sanzu Island tour — all three prefectures on Sanzu (Tosa, Naruto, Okayama) had now hosted a Wednesday night event. The show featured nine matches and was headlined by the first-ever tag team match between [[Leoni Masua]] & [[Taumafa Vaiahi]] — the Vaiahi family united against [[Kengo Vaiahi|Kengo]] & [[Malo Vaiahi|Malo]] of the [[Cannon Club]]. The event also featured the official contract signing for the [[IGO Heavyweight Championship]] match at [[Island Invasion Tour|Island Invasion]] between Leoni and [[KAZUKI (wrestler)|KAZUKI]], a fourth consecutive match-of-the-night candidate from [[Marcus Vance|Marcus \"The Drill\" Vance]] against [[Nakamura Shinsuke]], the [[IGO World Television Championship]] changing hands when [[Jin Tanaka|Jin \"Bulldog\" Tanaka]] defeated [[Tadayoshi Ishida]] to bring a fourth title into the [[Cannon Club]], and the return of eight wrestlers who had been absent from Episode 4.

== Background ==

Following [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 4]] on July 15 in [[Naruto, Naruto|Naruto]] — where Leoni Masua and Ryohei Maeda defeated Kengo and Malo cleanly, KAZUKI confronted Leoni post-match ("You don't need me. I saw."), Taumafa Vaiahi made his Wednesday night in-ring debut with a win over Big Stan, and Marcus Vance recorded his third consecutive match-of-the-night candidate against KAZUKI — NOPW moved its Wednesday night product east to [[Anjo-Saikawa]], the capital of [[Okayama Prefecture]] and the largest city on [[Sanzu]] Island (population 819,838). The Okayama Prefectural Arena (capacity 8,500) sold out in 18 hours — the fastest sellout in the Wednesday night product's history, breaking the 24-hour record set by Naruto the previous week. The fifth consecutive market and the fifth consecutive sellout confirmed the product was a phenomenon.

Key storylines entering Episode 5:
* The Kuroshio bond was officially fractured. KAZUKI had confronted Leoni at Episode 4 — "You don't need me. I saw." — and pushed aside Maeda, the mediator. The #1 contender was isolating himself. The IGO Heavyweight Championship match at Island Invasion was two weeks away and had not yet been officially signed.
* The Vaiahi family dynamic had escalated. Kengo had sent Big Stan to test Taumafa at Episode 4 — the giant failed. Taumafa challenged Kengo: "Send someone better than Big Stan." Kengo responded: "Family can be your worst enemy." The three Vaiahi — Leoni, Kengo, Taumafa — were now the second major storyline heading into Island Invasion.
* Marcus Vance had recorded three consecutive match-of-the-night candidates (Episode 2: Takagi Yuto, Episode 3: Daigo Kuroki, Episode 4: KAZUKI). The cool heel was the best worker in NOPW. The question: who could end the streak?
* [[Nakamura Shinsuke]] was 3-0 against Cannon Club members on the Wednesday product (Tanaka, Big Stan, Diallo). The unaffiliated veteran was one of the most popular acts. The question: who would be his next challenge?
* The [[Cannon Club]]'s mid-card crisis had deepened at Episode 4 — the faction went 1-4, with only Vance winning. The title-holders (Vance, the Usos) remained strong; the mid-card was in crisis. The faction needed its lower-card members to step up.
* [[Tadayoshi Ishida]] had retained the [[NOPW World Television Championship|World Television Championship]] against [[Yuto Ono]] at Episode 4 — the young lion's first title shot. Ishida raised Ono's hand post-match in a passing-of-the-torch moment. But the champion's next challenger was already circling: [[Jin Tanaka|Jin \"Bulldog\" Tanaka]], the Seigigun traitor who had joined the [[Cannon Club]] in 2019. Tanaka had lost to Ono at Episode 3 and been accidentally clotheslined by his own partner, The Marauder, at Episode 4. The Cannon Club brawler was due — and the title he was targeting belonged to his former faction. The personal stakes were clear: the traitor returns to take the title from the faction he betrayed.
* [[Yuto Ono]]'s three-match win streak had ended in a TV title loss to Tadayoshi Ishida at Episode 4, but the young lion earned the champion's respect and a standing ovation. Ono did not wrestle at Episode 5 — the young lion was resting after his first title shot. The question: what's next for the young lion?
* The [[The Marauder]]'s Wednesday night debut at Episode 4 was a disaster — he accidentally clotheslined his own partner, Jin Tanaka, and shoved him post-match. The question: could the wild man be controlled?
* [[Diego Reyes]] and [[Haruto Kimura]] had won the #1 contender's match at Episode 4 and would challenge the [[Usos]] for the [[IGO Tag Team Championship]] at Island Invasion. The Usos had not wrestled at Episode 4 — they watched the #1 contender's match from the backstage area.
* Eight wrestlers had been absent from Episode 4: [[Tanahashi Hiroshi]], [[Daigo Kuroki]], [[Kawada Masahiro]], [[Takagi Yuto]], [[Tetsuya Yamamoto|Yamamoto Tetsuya]], [[Katsuhiko Morita|Morita Katsuhiko]], [[Akira Sato|Sato Akira]], and the [[Usos]] (Tama and Riku Uso). All eight were expected to return at Episode 5.

