;Match details

* '''Match 1:''' Junior showcase. '''Face vs. face''' — Yamamoto (Seigigun) vs. Sato (CHAOS). Both returning after missing Episode 4. Yamamoto — coming off his first Wednesday night win at Episode 3 — vs. Sato — coming off a loss to Ono at Episode 3. A fast-paced junior match: Yamamoto's high-flying vs. Sato's second-generation technical game. Sato hit a beautiful dropkick sequence, but Yamamoto's speed was too much. Yamamoto hit a springboard DDT at 9:45 — his second consecutive win. The young high-flyer is building momentum. '''Crowd:''' POP for both entrances. "YAMAMOTO" chants. Applause for Sato's dropkick sequence. BIG POP for the springboard DDT. Respectful applause for both men post-match.
* '''Match 2:''' Redemption match. '''Heel vs. face''' — The Marauder (Unaffiliated) vs. Morita (Seigigun). Both returning after missing Episode 4. The Marauder — coming off a disastrous debut at Episode 4 where he accidentally clotheslined his own partner — was in a singles match this time. No partner to hit. No tags to miss. Just the wild man and his opponent. Morita — the rising Seigigun heavyweight — was the stepping stone. The Marauder was dominant. He brawled on the floor, but this time his chaos was directed at the opponent, not his own team. The running big boot — the same move that accidentally hit Tanaka at Episode 4 — connected cleanly at 8:22. The Marauder's first Wednesday night win. Dangerous when focused. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for The Marauder's entrance — the crowd remembers the debut disaster. "WHO ARE YOU?" chants. HEAT for the floor brawling. BIG POP for the running big boot — the same move, but this time it hit the right person. The Marauder stood over Morita post-match — no apology, no celebration. Just menace.
* '''Match 3:''' World TV title match. '''Heel vs. face''' — Tanaka (Cannon Club) vs. Ishida (c, Seigigun). The traitor returns. Jin "Bulldog" Tanaka — the Seigigun defector who joined the Cannon Club in 2019 — challenged his former faction's champion for the World Television Championship. The personal stakes were written on both faces: Ishida's quiet fury at the betrayal, Tanaka's cold satisfaction at the opportunity. The match was physical and bitter. Tanaka targeted Ishida's neck — the same area the champion had targeted against Ono at Episode 4. Ishida fought back with his technical precision, locking in the Ishida Lock at 9:30. Tanaka clawed to the ropes — barely. The crowd thought the champion had it. But Tanaka raked Ishida's eyes while the referee was checking on Tanaka's condition — a veteran cheap shot, invisible to the official. A stunned Ishida stumbled into the Bulldog Bomb — Tanaka's signature powerbomb — at 12:45. The traitor takes the title. The Cannon Club now holds four of the eight IGO championships. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for Tanaka's entrance — the crowd remembers the betrayal. POP for Ishida. "ISHIDA" chants. HEAT at the neck targeting. BIG POP for the Ishida Lock — the crowd thought it was over. TENSION as Tanaka reached the ropes. NUCLEAR HEAT at the eye rake — the crowd saw it, the referee didn't. NUCLEAR HEAT at the Bulldog Bomb finish. "BULLSHIT" chants. Tanaka snatched the title and held it over Ishida's fallen body. The Seigigun has been robbed.
* '''Match 4:''' Tag title match. '''Face vs. heel''' — Tanahashi & Kuroki (Seigigun) vs. The Usos (c, Cannon Club). The Usos' first Wednesday night defense since Episode 3. Tanahashi — the veteran former IGO Heavyweight Champion — and Kuroki — the former Kuroshio enforcer — were a thrown-together team, and it showed. The Usos' chemistry — eight title reigns, years of experience as a unit — was the difference. Tanahashi and Kuroki had moments of brilliance: Tanahashi's Sling Blade on Tama, Kuroki's Black Iron Clothesline on Riku. But the Usos' double-team game was too polished. At 18:40, Tama hit the Uso Splash on Kuroki — the tag champions retain. Post-match: [[Diego Reyes]] and [[Haruto Kimura]] appeared on the ramp. They pointed at the Usos. The challenge for Island Invasion was set. '''Crowd:''' MEGA POP for Tanahashi's entrance — the veteran is beloved. POP for Kuroki. HEAT for the Usos. "TANAHASHI" chants. BIG POP for the Sling Blade. BIG POP for the Black Iron Clothesline. HEAT at the Uso Splash finish. BIG POP for Reyes & Kimura's appearance — the crowd knows the Island Invasion match is set.
* '''Match 5:''' Tag team grudge match. '''Face vs. heel''' — Kawada & Takagi (CHAOS) vs. Big Stan & Diallo (Cannon Club). Both teams returning after missing Episode 4. The CHAOS strong style team — Kawada's brutal strikes and Takagi's Made in Nakamizu lariat — vs. the Cannon Club power team — Big Stan's 160 kg frame and Diallo's 130 kg hammering. A physical, hard-hitting match. Kawada and Takagi's striking was too sharp for the power team. Kawada hit a brainbuster on Diallo at 13:15 — CHAOS wins. The Cannon Club's mid-card crisis continues. '''Crowd:''' POP for CHAOS entrance. HEAT for the Cannon Club. "KAWADA" chants. GASPS at the power spots — Big Stan's body slam on Takagi shook the ring. BIG POP for the brainbuster finish. Boos at the Cannon Club's post-match frustration.
* '''Match 6:''' Strong Openweight title match. '''Face vs. face''' — Taumafa (c, Independent) vs. Honda (Unaffiliated). Taumafa's second Wednesday night title defense. The Strong Openweight Champion vs. the AOPW representative — the independent Vaiahi warrior vs. the son of Honda "The Shogun" Tadakatsu. A clash of traditions: Vaiahi island grappling vs. AOPW methodical power. Honda's German suplex game was sharp — he bridged for 2.5 at one point. But Taumafa's power and fighting spirit were too much. The Samoan Spike at 14:50 — the champion retains. Post-match: Honda raised Taumafa's hand — respect between two warriors. '''Crowd:''' MEGA POP for Taumafa. POP for Honda. "TAUMAFA" chants. GASPS at the German suplex bridge near-fall. MEGA POP for the Samoan Spike. Respectful applause for Honda post-match.
* '''Match 7:''' IC title match. '''Heel vs. tweener''' — Vance (c, Cannon Club) vs. Nakamura (independent). Vance's fourth consecutive match-of-the-night candidate. The best worker in NOPW vs. the unaffiliated veteran who was 3-0 against the Cannon Club. The match was a masterpiece — Vance's technical precision vs. Nakamura's unorthodox, charismatic style. Nakamura hit the first Boma Ye — Vance kicked out at 2.5. The crowd erupted. Vance hit the Drill Driver — Nakamura kicked out at 2.5. The crowd gasped. Nakamura went for a second Boma Ye — Vance ducked, hit a German suplex hold for 2.5. The arena was shaking. Vance hit a second Drill Driver — Nakamura was done at 24:18. Four title defenses, four match-of-the-night candidates, four standing ovations. The cool heel is unstoppable. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for Vance's entrance. MEGA POP for Nakamura's entrance. "NAKAMURA" chants. "THIS IS AWESOME" chants. MEGA POP for the Boma Ye kick-out. GASPS at the Drill Driver kick-out. NUCLEAR POP for the German suplex near-fall. Boos at the finish. STANDING OVATION for both men. "THIS IS WRESTLING" chants. Four MOTNs. The streak is unprecedented.
* '''Match 8:''' Singles showcase. '''Tweener vs. face''' — KAZUKI (Independent) vs. Tiger Mask (Fifth, Unaffiliated). The #1 contender for the IGO Heavyweight Championship vs. the masked tradition. KAZUKI was coming off a loss to Vance and a confrontation with Leoni at Episode 4. He needed a win. Tiger Mask — coming off a debut win over El Santo Oro at Episode 4 — was stepping up in competition. The match was fast-paced and competitive: KAZUKI's aerial game vs. Tiger Mask's technical mat wrestling. Tiger Mask hit the Tiger Driver for 2.5 — the crowd gasped. KAZUKI answered with the Twin Star Press at 16:30 — clean win. The #1 contender is back on track. Post-match: KAZUKI took the mic. '''Crowd:''' BIG POP for KAZUKI's entrance. POP for Tiger Mask. "KAZUKI" chants. GASPS at the Tiger Driver kick-out. MEGA POP for the Twin Star Press. Respectful applause for Tiger Mask. Then — silence as KAZUKI takes the mic.
* '''Match 9:''' Main event tag match. '''Face vs. heel''' — Leoni Masua & Taumafa Vaiahi vs. Kengo & Malo (Cannon Club). The first-ever tag team match between Leoni and Taumafa — the Vaiahi family united. The question: could the IGO Heavyweight Champion and the Strong Openweight Champion coexist? Kengo tried to exploit the tension — he targeted Taumafa, trying to drive a wedge between the two Vaiahi. But Leoni and Taumafa found common ground. They're both Vaiahi. They both fight with the same warrior spirit. Taumafa's Samoan Spike on Malo created the opening. Leoni hit the Spear of Fangatapu on Malo at 21:45. Clean, decisive. The Vaiahi family stands together — against Kengo. '''Crowd:''' NUCLEAR POP for Leoni's entrance. MEGA POP for Taumafa's entrance. "VAIAHI" chants — the first time the crowd chanted the family name. NUCLEAR HEAT for Kengo & Malo. "LEONI" chants. BIG POP when Taumafa and Leoni fist-bumped before the match. TENSION when Kengo targeted Taumafa. MEGA POP for the Samoan Spike. NUCLEAR POP for the Spear of Fangatapu finish. The crowd roars.

== Post-match segment: The Contract Signing ==

=== Leoni and Taumafa celebrate ===

The bell rings. Leoni Masua and Taumafa Vaiahi stand in the ring. The Okayama crowd is on its feet. For the first time, the Vaiahi family stands together — Leoni, the IGO Heavyweight Champion, and Taumafa, the Strong Openweight Champion. They fist-bump in the center of the ring. The crowd chants '''VAIAHI'''.

Taumafa takes the mic:

:''"Kengo. You said family can be your worst enemy. You're right. But family can also be your worst nightmare."'' — HUGE POP

Leoni takes the mic:

:''"Two weeks. Fangatapu. The Chief walks in champion. The Chief walks out champion."'' — HUGE POP

=== KAZUKI's promo ===

Then — KAZUKI's music hits. The crowd ERUPTS. The #1 contender walks out. He has a mic. He doesn't enter the ring — he stands on the ramp.

KAZUKI looks at Leoni in the ring. Then at Taumafa. Then back at Leoni.

:''"Enjoy the moment, Chief. Enjoy the family. The fist-bump. The VAIAHI chants. The bond."'' — Pause. — ''"Because in two weeks, there's no bond. There's no family. There's no Kuroshio. There's just you and me. One on one. And I'm not Big Stan. I'm not Malo. I'm not Kengo."'' — HUGE POP

:''"I'm the Shooting Star. And at Fangatapu, I'm taking that title."'' — MEGA POP

The crowd is split — half chanting '''TRIBAL CHIEF''', half chanting '''KAZUKI'''. The tension is thick.

=== The contract signing ===

The ring announcer calls for the official contract signing. A table is set up in the ring with two chairs. The [[IGO Heavyweight Championship]] contract is on the table. The match: Leoni Masua (c) vs. KAZUKI, Island Invasion Tour, August 9, 2026, Fangatapu, Vaiahi Islands.

KAZUKI enters the ring. He sits down. He doesn't look at Leoni.

Leoni sits down. He doesn't look at KAZUKI.

The official reads the contract terms. Both men listen in silence.

KAZUKI signs first. He doesn't hesitate. He signs and pushes the contract across the table.

Leoni signs. He looks at KAZUKI for the first time. The tension is palpable.

Leoni takes the mic:

:''"KAZUKI. We were brothers. Kuroshio. The Black Tide. And now —"''

KAZUKI takes the mic:

:''"And now I'm going to take your title. I don't need brothers. I don't need the Black Tide. I need that belt."'' — HUGE POP

Leoni stands up. KAZUKI stands up. They're face to face. The crowd is split — '''TRIBAL CHIEF''' vs. '''KAZUKI'''. Neither man blinks.

=== Maeda's intervention ===

Then — Ryohei Maeda's music hits. POP. The Kuroshio mediator walks out. He has a mic.

:''"Both of you, listen to me. You were brothers. You were Kuroshio. You don't have to —"''

KAZUKI flips the table. He doesn't want mediation. He doesn't want to hear about brotherhood. He wants Leoni.

=== The brawl ===

KAZUKI lunges at Leoni. They brawl. Officials storm the ring. Taumafa watches from the corner — he doesn't intervene. This isn't his fight.

Leoni and KAZUKI are separated by officials. The crowd is split — half chanting '''TRIBAL CHIEF''', half chanting '''KAZUKI'''. The tension is at its peak.

=== Kengo's gloating ===

Then — Kengo's music hits. NUCLEAR HEAT. The Cannon Club leader walks out with Malo and Marcus Vance. He has a mic. He's smiling.

:''"Look at you. The Kuroshio brothers. The bond. The brotherhood."'' — Kengo laughs. — ''"The bond is dead. The brotherhood is dead. And the Cannon Club — we took the World TV title tonight. We hold four belts. Half the gold in this promotion sits in the Cannon Club. And at Fangatapu, the Chief and the Shooting Star will kill each other. And the Cannon Club will be there to pick up the pieces."'' — HEAT

Kengo smiles. Cold. He backs up the ramp.

=== Closing image ===

In the ring: Leoni Masua and KAZUKI, separated by officials. The contract is signed. The match is official. The table is overturned.

At the ramp: Kengo — smiling. Malo and Vance flanking him. The Cannon Club leader has the psychological edge. The dysfunction is exactly what he wanted.

At the top of the ramp: Taumafa — independent. The Strong Openweight Champion watches. The Vaiahi family is divided.

On the stage: Ryohei Maeda — the mediator. The man who held the Kuroshio bond together. The table is flipped. The bond is broken. There is nothing left to mediate.

The contract is signed. The match is official. The war is coming to Fangatapu.

Cut to black.

