== Storyline notes ==

* '''The Vaiahi family stands together.''' For the first time, Leoni Masua and Taumafa Vaiahi teamed up — the IGO Heavyweight Champion and the Strong Openweight Champion, united against Kengo and Malo. The crowd chanted '''VAIAHI''' — the first time the family name was chanted. The fist-bump before the match was the moment: two independent warriors, both champions, choosing to stand together against the Cannon Club. Taumafa's post-match promo — "Family can also be your worst nightmare" — confirmed that his independence didn't mean isolation. He stands with Leoni against Kengo. The Vaiahi family dynamic is now the second major storyline heading into Island Invasion.
* '''The contract signing.''' The IGO Heavyweight Championship match at Island Invasion was officially signed. KAZUKI signed without hesitation — he doesn't need ceremony, he needs the match. Leoni signed with weight — he knows what this match means. The moment KAZUKI flipped the table was the moment the Kuroshio bond officially died. Maeda came out to mediate — KAZUKI flipped the table before he could finish. The mediator has nothing left to mediate. The bond is broken. The match is official. Fangatapu is coming.
* '''KAZUKI's isolation.''' KAZUKI beat Tiger Mask cleanly, then cut a promo from the ramp — he didn't enter the ring until the contract signing. He didn't want to celebrate with Leoni and Taumafa. He didn't want to fist-bump. He didn't want the VAIAHI chants. He wanted the contract signed and the match made. His promo — "I'm not Big Stan. I'm not Kengo. I'm the Shooting Star." — was a declaration: he is not a side character in the Vaiahi family drama. He is the main event. The #1 contender is alone, and that isolation is his identity now.
* '''Vance's fourth consecutive MOTN.''' Marcus Vance's match with Nakamura was the match of the night — his fourth consecutive match-of-the-night candidate (Episode 2: Takagi Yuto, Episode 3: Daigo Kuroki, Episode 4: KAZUKI, Episode 5: Nakamura). The German suplex hold near-fall was the most dramatic moment of the match — the arena shook. The cool heel dynamic is now the most unique crowd reaction in NOPW: heat for the man, standing ovation for the match. Four title defenses, four standing ovations. The streak is unprecedented. The question heading into Island Invasion: who can end it?
* '''Nakamura's streak ends.''' Nakamura Shinsuke's 3-0 run against the Cannon Club ended with a loss to Vance — but it took a second Drill Driver to put him down. The loss was understandable: Vance is the IC champion and the best worker in NOPW. Nakamura kicked out of the first Drill Driver — something no one else had done. The unaffiliated veteran proved he can hang with the best, and the standing ovation after the match confirmed the crowd's respect. The question: what's next for Nakamura?
* '''The traitor takes the title.''' Jin "Bulldog" Tanaka — the Seigigun defector who joined the Cannon Club in 2019 — defeated Tadayoshi Ishida for the World Television Championship. The match was personal: the traitor returning to take the title from the faction he betrayed. Ishida had the champion's respect after his Episode 4 defense against Ono, but Tanaka stole the victory with a hidden eye rake followed by the Bulldog Bomb. The Cannon Club now holds four of the eight IGO championships: the Intercontinental (Vance), the Tag Team (Usos), the Junior Tag Team (Kai & Viggo), and the World Television (Tanaka). The faction's title war is succeeding. The Seigigun has been robbed — and the question is whether they can fight back at Island Invasion.
* '''The Marauder redeems.''' After his disastrous debut at Episode 4, The Marauder returned in a singles match and defeated Morita cleanly with the running big boot — the same move that accidentally hit Tanaka. This time, it hit the right person. The Marauder is dangerous when focused — the question is whether he can stay focused in a tag team. The post-match image — standing over Morita without celebration — confirmed: this is not a man who celebrates. This is a man who destroys.
* '''The Usos retain.''' The 8-time tag champions defended against the thrown-together team of Tanahashi and Kuroki. The veterans had moments — Tanahashi's Sling Blade, Kuroki's Black Iron Clothesline — but the Usos' chemistry was too much. Post-match, Diego Reyes and Haruto Kimura appeared on the ramp, pointing at the champions. The Island Invasion tag title match is set: the Cobra and the Wind vs. the 8-time kings. The Usos have been warned.
* '''Cannon Club's winning night.''' The Cannon Club's record at Episode 5 was 3-2 — Vance, the Usos, and Tanaka won; Big Stan and Diallo lost. The title-holders all retained, and Tanaka captured the World Television Championship from Ishida. The faction now holds four of the eight IGO championships — half the titles in the promotion. Kengo's declaration of war on all eight IGO championships is succeeding at the top. The mid-card continues to struggle — Big Stan and Diallo lost again — but the title haul masks the depth problem. The question heading into Island Invasion: can the Cannon Club defend all four titles, or will the mid-card weakness finally cost them?
* '''The Okayama Prefectural Arena sellout.''' The 8,500-seat arena sold out in 18 hours — breaking the 24-hour record set by Naruto the previous week. The step from Nagayama (4,200) to Kurosaki (6,500) to Tosa (6,000) to Naruto (7,500) to Okayama (8,500) confirmed the product was growing. The fifth consecutive market, the fifth consecutive sellout. The Sanzu Island tour is complete — all three prefectures (Tosa, Naruto, Okayama) have hosted a Wednesday night event. Wednesday nights are the hottest ticket in Okaiken.

