== Aftermath ==

* The contract signing for the IGO Heavyweight Championship match at Island Invasion was completed. Leoni Masua vs. KAZUKI, August 9, 2026, Fangatapu, Vaiahi Islands. The match is official. KAZUKI's table flip — the moment the Kuroshio bond officially died — was the emotional climax of the episode and the defining image of the build to Fangatapu. Maeda's attempt at mediation was rejected before it began. The mediator has nothing left to mediate. The bond is broken. The war is coming.
* The Vaiahi family tag team match was a success — Leoni and Taumafa defeated Kengo and Malo, and the crowd chanted '''VAIAHI''' for the first time. The fist-bump before the match was the moment: two independent champions choosing to stand together. Taumafa's post-match promo — "Family can also be your worst nightmare" — confirmed that his independence doesn't mean isolation. He stands with Leoni against Kengo. The Vaiahi family dynamic — Leoni, Kengo, Taumafa — is now the second major storyline heading into Island Invasion, alongside the Leoni-KAZUKI dysfunction.
* Marcus Vance's fourth consecutive match-of-the-night candidate — this time against Nakamura Shinsuke — extended the unprecedented streak. The German suplex hold near-fall was the most dramatic moment: the arena shook. Nakamura kicked out of the first Drill Driver — something no one else had done — but the second put him down. Four title defenses, four standing ovations. The cool heel is the best worker in NOPW, and the crowd knows it. The question heading into Island Invasion: who can end the streak? And does Vance have a fourth title defense in him at Fangatapu?
* Nakamura Shinsuke's 3-0 run against the Cannon Club ended with a loss to Vance, but the unaffiliated veteran proved he can hang with the best. The standing ovation after the match confirmed the crowd's respect. The question: what's next for Nakamura? He's unaffiliated, he's popular, and he's proven he can hang with the IC champion. Could he challenge for the Strong Openweight Championship? Could he be a wild card at Island Invasion?
* Jin "Bulldog" Tanaka — the Seigigun traitor — defeated Tadayoshi Ishida for the World Television Championship with a hidden eye rake and the Bulldog Bomb. The Cannon Club now holds four of the eight IGO championships: the Intercontinental (Vance), the Tag Team (Usos), the Junior Tag Team (Kai & Viggo), and the World Television (Tanaka). Half the titles in the promotion. Kengo's declaration of war on all eight IGO championships is succeeding at the top. The Seigigun has been robbed — the traitor took the title from the faction he betrayed. The question heading into Island Invasion: can the Seigigun fight back, or is the Cannon Club's grip on the titles too strong?
* The Marauder redeemed himself with a clean win over Morita — the running big boot, the same move that accidentally hit Tanaka, connected with the right person this time. The wild man is dangerous when focused. The question: can he be focused in a tag team? Or is he strictly a singles competitor? The Marauder's post-match image — standing over Morita without celebration — confirmed: this is not a man who celebrates. This is a man who destroys.
* The Usos retained the IGO Tag Team Championship against the thrown-together team of Tanahashi and Kuroki. The 8-time champions' chemistry was too much for the veterans. Post-match, Diego Reyes and Haruto Kimura appeared on the ramp, pointing at the champions. The Island Invasion tag title match is set: the Cobra and the Wind vs. the 8-time kings. The Usos have been warned.
* The Cannon Club's record at Episode 5 was 3-2 — Vance, the Usos, and Tanaka won; Big Stan and Diallo lost. The faction captured the World Television Championship and now holds four of the eight IGO championships — half the titles in the promotion. The title-holders all retained, and Tanaka's victory gave the Cannon Club a winning night. However, the mid-card continues to struggle — Big Stan and Diallo lost again. The faction's depth problem persists beneath the title haul. The question heading into Island Invasion: can the Cannon Club defend all four titles, or will the mid-card weakness finally cost them?
* The Okayama Prefectural Arena sellout (8,500) — the fastest in Wednesday night history at 18 hours — confirmed the fifth consecutive market for the touring product. The step from Nagayama (4,200) to Kurosaki (6,500) to Tosa (6,000) to Naruto (7,500) to Okayama (8,500) showed the product was growing. The Sanzu Island tour is complete — all three prefectures (Tosa, Naruto, Okayama) have hosted a Wednesday night event. The next stop — and the go-home show for Island Invasion — is to be announced.

